    "turn_text": "out if you don't do the right thing. I think this is one of those moments where particularly all members of the caucus have responsibility to make their own judgment about what they think is best for the country, what the evidence provides, what they think is the best course of action. I think it's important you cannot have a president engage in persistent misconduct and then thwart the oversight of Congress as it relates to that conduct and not be held accountable. The American people elect us, we got the house back for two reasons. One, because we promise to deliver on our for-the-people agenda, driving down healthcare costs, raising family incomes by rebuilding the infrastructure of America, and taking on the corruption and self-dealing in Washington. We're delivering on those. The other reason we got the House back is because the American people wanted us to hold this president accountable. They expect us to do both things, and I feel very strongly you cannot. This is not just about President Trump. This is also about future presidents who are watching this lawless president not being held accountable",
