    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/1/91092.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 26,
    "turn_text": "Yes, I am. And I'll tell you this. There are a number of people who didn't vote for that resolution in part because it referenced the president's racist comments when they are deplorable and disgraceful. And one of the worst things I've seen him do in terms of stuff he said, those are not actually impeachable offenses. So there are a lot of people who said, look, we need to refer this to the Judiciary Committee because that's the Committee of Jurisdiction. You're already reviewing a whole range of issues. But being a racist sadly is not an impeachable offense. So I don't think you can read too much. We're seeing a number of people from swing districts who have come out for the opening of an impeachment inquiry because I think they're hearing it from their constituents.",
