    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/1/91092.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 28,
    "turn_text": "It's disappointing. I think that was one of the most disgusting, horrible things I've seen the president do. In evidences, most importantly, that the president doesn't understand what has made our country great and the envy of the world. And that is that people from all over the world come to America and try to build a better lives from themselves and their family. and that we have a set of shared values, our commitment to human dignity, to justice for all, to freedom, to opportunity. You know, many generations of Americans, Italian Americans, Irish Americans, Polish Americans, they all heard the same thing. Go back where you came from. That is so un-American. It undermines the founding values of this country. It's not who we are. It was a disgraceful display of racism and to see others chanting with him I think was really disappointing. Now the president I think heard from even Republican colleagues in the Congress apparently heard from his daughter that this was just had gone too far and so now he's trying to sort of backpell and say well I I didn't really mean it I tried to speak quickly we know that's not true if you watch the tape he waited 13 full seconds before he started again he said exactly the same thing on Twitter so it's it's his message but Look, this is a very dangerous time we're living in, where the kind of rule of law, the founding values of our country, where the understanding that our diversity is a great strength of America, are being challenged by this president. And we all have a responsibility to stand up and condemn this racism as loudly and powerfully as we can.",
