    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/1/91092.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 30,
    "turn_text": "Yeah, no, no. I don't know if it was a shot at the Speaker, but the Speaker, I think, and I have disagreed on the opening of an impeachment inquiry. We've had a lively discussion about it. I have one view. I think the time has come to open in Korea. I think the Speaker has been very clear that she does not think that that's appropriate to do at this point. I am a member of the leadership team and have always felt the strength I bring to it is not only that Rhode Island's at the leadership table, but that I have the opportunity to share my best thinking. And Speaker Pelosi has always encouraged us to do that. I responded to the speaker by explaining, every time I talk about the impeachment inquiry, I also talk about the importance of reinforcing the work we're getting down for the American people. We have to",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_01",
    "inferred_speaker_name": null,
    "inferred_speaker_role": null,
    "chosen_text_key": "transcript",
    "explicit_propositions": [
