    "turn_idx": 37,
    "turn_text": "No, you know, it's interesting. I know it gets reported as if there's some division in the Democratic caucus. It's interesting. We have the largest caucus we've ever had with the greatest diversity we've ever had. And, you know, everyone brings their passions and their ideas and their priorities to that caucus, and some people prioritize this and have this view of that. And out of this, we build consensus as a Democratic caucus. That is exactly how the process is supposed to work. And a lot of it is out in the open, and there's disagreements about what's the best way to proceed on healthcare or on infrastructure bill. But that's what the benefit of having a big, diverse caucus is. And the good news is we reach consensus and we've been able to move forward as a caucus on 50 major pieces of legislation over 230 in total that will make a real difference in people's lives as the Senate Majority Leader will take them up.",
