    "turn_idx": 70,
    "turn_text": "So let me just push back for a second about the dividing of Democrats. It is true that in the Democratic caucus and among some Democratic presidential candidates, there are a variety of different ideas that range from Medicare for all to Medicare for all who want it, to buy into Medicare, to lower the age of Medicare, to a public option, and a whole range of others. And those are all about expanding coverage and driving down costs. On the Republican side, the president of the United States is in court with the Republican governors of this country in the Fifth Circuit trying to take away health care in its entirety, have the Affordable Care Act declared unconstitutional. Millions of people will lose coverage for preexisting conditions, they will lose their subsidies, and they will decimate the health care system. So the difference between Republicans and Democrats is very, very serious. Among the Democrats, this is a bunch of good ideas. And so I think the system will end up with a private insurance option and some expanded use to Medicare.",
