    "turn_idx": 72,
    "turn_text": "Buttigieg says, yeah, Medicare for everyone who wants that kind of model. But I think the important thing is, there's a lot of play about the differences on the edges between some of these expansions. But the real difference is between what Democrats are fighting for and what the Republicans are doing, voting to repeal it in its entirety, sabotaging the Affordable Care Act, and trying to take away coverage pre-existing conditions. We shouldn't lose sight of that. I think the agenda that Democrats are really unified on is making certain that we drive down the cost of prescription drugs. That is one of the principal drivers of health care costs. We have a number of pieces of legislation. We've already passed out of the house that will significantly reduce prescription drug prices. One of them is my bill, the Creates Act. to make it easier to get to network drugs to market. So there's real consensus on driving down the cost of prescription drugs. And there's real consensus on fortifying the coverage for pre-existing conditions. And I think the Democrats will have a real debate about which of these proposals gets us there in terms of a public option, lowering the age of Medicare and the like. But I think we have a lot of work to do. We're going to have hearings and there's going to be a lot of debate. And I think we'll have the benefit of people you know, contributing their best thinking on this. And we'll arrive at a solution. And that'll be governed a lot by who our president is in 2020. That individual obviously lead on which of these",
