    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/1/91092.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 81,
    "turn_text": "Well, don't forget, this is a hearing which is part of a larger investigation that we launched. The Judiciary Committee launched that being led by the antitrust subcommittee. And this is a broad look at the digital marketplace and to see kind of what the absence of competition means, the sort of monopolies that exist. discriminatory or anti-competitive behavior. So we're just in the very early stages of the investigation. And Congress doesn't have a role in breaking up companies, but what is clear is that these platforms, particularly platforms like Amazon and Facebook, they are essentially operating like monopolies with enormous market power. they're engaged in some discriminatory behavior, favoring their own products and services, prioritizing their placement on the platforms and",
