    "turn_idx": 83,
    "turn_text": "if you go into CVS, it's not like CVS brand next to a name brand. It's like the CVS brand is here and the name brand is up three flights and there's no ladder. I mean, you can't actually find it. So it's different. I don't know if that analogy is quite true, but I get your point. But the point is, one mix of these people like Amazon. So, but here's the thing, people like Amazon, I like Amazon, that's not the question. Yes, I am, but here's the question. What Amazon does is they, they mine the data, so they look at what's the hot item, it's a greenwood table. And then they create a greenwood table on their private label. And they put that on their website, they prioritize the Amazon buybacks for the greenwood table. Guess what, the guy in Vermont making a greenwood table, he's on third page. They put him on a business. So those sort of anti-competitive behaviors we need to know about, A, because it's reducing innovation, startups, entrepreneurship. It's creating an inability for people to create the next new Facebook, the next new Amazon, the next new Google. We want to make sure the market is working and there's competition so that new entrants into the market for the next new product, the next platform will have a reasonable chance of success.",
